Trace shutdown coverage
=======================

shutdown_test calls the production shutdown helper with injected monotonic
clock, kevent, signal and reap operations. It covers failure to establish the
grace deadline, failure while checking it, normal remaining-time calculation,
and interrupted final reaping. Real descriptors stand in for process and
liveness handles so their closure is verified. These are control-flow tests,
not proof of real protected-worker termination or a wall-clock shutdown bound.

session_test exercises real channel sessions on the native guest. Full bundle
admission, actual tracing-device teardown, parent-liveness behavior, and
SwitchBoard acknowledgement ordering remain separate integration gates.
The five-second graceful phase and per-worker liveness sockets differ from
Device/Crypto's immediate cleanup, so they must be preserved in any further
shared-library extraction.

shutdown_reports_cleanup_failure injects failed forced termination and final
reaping. It verifies first-error preservation, nonblocking remaining waits,
and closure of both process and liveness descriptors. Actual termination
denial and supervisor recovery of surviving protected workers remain full
integration checks.

exit_event_reap_errors injects an exit event during graceful shutdown and
checks retry after EINTR, propagation of EIO, and acceptance of ECHILD and ESRCH. It
verifies list/count cleanup and actual FD closure without sending SIGKILL to
a child whose exit event was observed. Kernel event delivery and real reap
failure remain separate integration checks.
